      "bucket": "security-deep",
      "subject": "fix(material/progress-bar): avoid CSP issues for apps not using buffer mode (#28946)",
      "final_disposition": "already-adapted",
      "reason": "The complete one-file/one-hunk non-buffer CSP fix is satisfied through two distinct preserved boundaries. Owned Material16 legacy progress markup uses an inline SVG pattern and never a current MDC buffer-dot element. The exported ordinary companion theme remains reachable, so legacy markup alone cannot exclude the change: both advertised minimum public MatProgressBar implementations create dots only in buffer mode. The owned companion still emits historical background CSS, including its inactive IE-only data URI, and the ordinary current component supplies its structural gradient. Require actual current packed Sass plus public current/legacy controls in both Angular runtime modes, all four progress modes, no positive image-policy violations and a real blocked-data-image negative. No template/style migration, current private machinery or ordinary component fork is introduced. Source identity is conditional evidence; complete native artifact admission and all global release gates remain mandatory.",
      "read_note_disposition": "unaffected",
